<title>NORWAY: Hydro takes stake in African metals firm.</title>
<headline>Hydro takes stake in African metals firm.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hydro Aluminium, a division of Norsk Hydro ASA, said on Friday it had begun negotiations to to buy a 30 percent stake in South African group Hulett Aluminium (Pty) Ltd.</p>
<p>The partners intend to establish a new company Hulett-Hydro Extrusions, which will begin operation in April. The venture will have three plants and six presses with a total capacity of 18,000 tonnes per year.</p>
<p>The new company will also take over Hulett's conductor and wire activities.</p>
<p>Hydro said the new venture would be a part of its Hydro Aluminium Extrusion business.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
